WEBVTT - MR. MAS Ep1 Act Four v5, plain SDH captions (English)

NOTE clock: act (offset +0.000 s from the act clock). Generated by captions/tools/build_access.py from show/reel/ep01-act4-v5.json; do not hand-edit.

sfx-01
00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:07.333
[waltz music]

a5-25-01
00:00:07.375 --> 00:00:09.458
Three of us stepped down this year.

a5-25-02
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:13.250
Leave out Mas and Gerg,
and the four of us are a majority.

a5-25-03
00:00:13.333 --> 00:00:17.208
This board controls the company.
Not the other way round.

a5-25-04
00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:22.625
Our biggest investor has put in billions.
It gets this many votes.

a5-25-05
00:00:22.708 --> 00:00:25.125
And the CEO? What does he own?

a5-25-06
00:00:25.375 --> 00:00:26.792
MADA: Good question.

sfx-02
00:00:31.167 --> 00:00:32.417
[music winds down]

sfx-03
00:00:41.583 --> 00:00:45.208
[click, then silence]

sfx-04
00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.125
[phone buzzes]

a5-26-01
00:00:47.417 --> 00:00:48.583
MAS: Super.

a5-26a-01
00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.125
MAS (voice-over): I don't keep score.

sfx-05
00:01:04.375 --> 00:01:05.375
[call chime]

a5-27-01.1
00:01:05.417 --> 00:01:10.042
ALYI: Mas. The board has decided that
you will no longer lead the company.

a5-27-01.2
00:01:10.125 --> 00:01:12.833
It will be announced shortly.

a5-27-02
00:01:13.625 --> 00:01:15.958
Do you have any questions?

a5-27-03
00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:18.625
NELEH: Is his feed frozen?

a5-27-04
00:01:18.708 --> 00:01:21.875
ALYI: No. That is just him.

a5-27-05
00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:25.507
MAS (through the laptop): Super.

a5-27-06
00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:31.000
NELEH: Step two.
I'll read it once before it goes up.

a5-27-07.1
00:01:31.083 --> 00:01:35.292
…he was not consistently candid in
his communications with the board…

a5-27-07.2
00:01:35.375 --> 00:01:40.625
The board no longer has confidence in
his ability to continue leading NopeAI.

a5-27-08
00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:42.333
Any objections?

sfx-06
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:44.833
[click; chime]

a5-27-09.1
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:45.708
Step three.

a5-27-09.2
00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:50.000
Rima, thank you for agreeing to serve
as interim CEO while we search.

a5-27-10
00:01:50.083 --> 00:01:51.167
RIMA: For how long?

a5-27-11
00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.125
NELEH: Until the search is done.

a5-27-12
00:01:53.208 --> 00:01:56.333
ALYI: The staff will
ask you what happened.

a5-27-13
00:01:56.417 --> 00:01:57.958
RIMA: What should I tell them?

a5-27-14
00:01:58.042 --> 00:02:01.542
NELEH: What the post says.
That's all the board is saying for now.

a5-27-15
00:02:01.625 --> 00:02:03.208
RIMA: We'll share more soon.

a5-27-16
00:02:03.292 --> 00:02:04.375
NELEH: Will we?

a5-27-17
00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.208
RIMA: More. Soon.

sfx-07
00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:07.500
[crowd hushes]

a5-27-18
00:02:07.542 --> 00:02:10.600
EMPLOYEE: Is this a coup?
Because it looks like one.

a5-27-19.1
00:02:11.042 --> 00:02:14.792
ALYI: You can call it this way…
I disagree with this.

a5-27-19.2
00:02:14.875 --> 00:02:19.417
This was the board doing its duty
to the mission of the nonprofit…

a5-27-20.1
00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.292
NELEH: Nobody asked him to go.

a5-27-20.2
00:02:24.375 --> 00:02:27.125
He'd have kept his job,
just not the chair.

a5-27-21
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:30.667
ALYI: Gerg has never waited to be asked.

sfx-08
00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:37.208
[phones buzz]

a5-27-22.1
00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:42.167
They're all asking whether it was allowed.
It was. The charter, footnote three.

a5-27-22.2
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:44.458
I've read it four times tonight.

a5-27-23.1
00:02:45.292 --> 00:02:48.667
What they actually want
to know is what happens on Monday.

a5-27-23.2
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.279
I'd like to be able
to tell them something.

a5-27-24
00:02:51.667 --> 00:02:54.583
ALYI: Step four will reveal itself.

a5-27-25
00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:55.708
NELEH: When?

a5-27-26
00:02:55.792 --> 00:02:58.333
ALYI: The company will tell us.

a5-27-27.1
00:02:58.417 --> 00:02:59.958
NELEH: That isn't a time, Alyi.

a5-27-27.2
00:03:00.042 --> 00:03:03.375
All we've given the staff
since yesterday is more soon.

a5-27-28
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.083
[phone clatters]
ALYI: That is the company telling us.

a5-27-29
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.338
NELEH: Then we'll write
step four ourselves.

sfx-10
00:03:11.422 --> 00:03:15.083
[dialing; phone rings]

a5-27-30.1
00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:19.292
Mario, it's Neleh, from the NopeAI board.
I'll be direct.

a5-27-30.2
00:03:19.375 --> 00:03:24.083
The board is offering you the job of CEO,
and it wants to discuss a merger.

a5-27-31.1
00:03:24.167 --> 00:03:25.750
MARIO: Neleh, hi. Wow.

a5-27-31.2
00:03:25.833 --> 00:03:28.417
I've actually written up some
thoughts on exactly this.

a5-27-31.3
00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.375
Eleven pages, on the conditions under
which we might, hypothetically—

a5-27-32
00:03:31.458 --> 00:03:33.542
ADELINA: In plain English: no.

sfx-11
00:03:33.625 --> 00:03:34.917
[dial tone; phone rings]

a5-27-33
00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.958
It's Nozama. About the money.

a5-27-34
00:03:37.042 --> 00:03:39.708
MARIO: Hi. Yes. We're very worried.
How much?

a5-27-35.1
00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.750
NELEH: He's been in
the building for hours.

a5-27-35.2
00:03:45.833 --> 00:03:49.625
We've talked all day about him
coming back, and we're no closer.

a5-27-36
00:03:49.792 --> 00:03:52.167
ALYI: They gave him a guest badge.

a5-27-37
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:55.309
NELEH: It's the correct badge.
He doesn't work here.

a5-27-38
00:04:00.667 --> 00:04:03.417
Ttemme, we'd like you
to serve as interim CEO.

a5-27-39
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.667
You already have an interim CEO.

a5-27-40
00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:07.458
We'd like a different one.

a5-27-41
00:04:07.625 --> 00:04:11.792
Fine. But before I say yes,
I need to know why you fired him.

a5-27-42
00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:15.375
Okay.

a5-27-43
00:04:16.125 --> 00:04:18.042
Chat… for how long?

sfx-12
00:04:21.792 --> 00:04:23.958
[keys jingle]

a5-27-44
00:04:24.042 --> 00:04:26.917
Good evening.
You'll want to hear our statement.

a5-27-45.1
00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.500
We look forward to getting to know Ttemme

a5-27-45.2
00:04:28.583 --> 00:04:31.667
and NopeAI's new leadership
team and working with them.

a5-27-45.3
00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:35.667
And we're extremely excited to share the
news that Mas Manalt and Gerg Mockbran,

a5-27-45.4
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:38.458
together with colleagues,
will be joining Macrosoft

a5-27-45.5
00:04:38.542 --> 00:04:41.458
to lead a new advanced AI research team.

a5-27-46
00:04:45.292 --> 00:04:46.583
NELEH: Step four?

a5-29-01
00:04:58.625 --> 00:05:00.583
The badge was a joke.

a5-29-02
00:05:01.125 --> 00:05:02.375
Mostly.

sfx-13
00:05:02.917 --> 00:05:04.208
[call rings]

a5-29-03
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.833
GERG: Sorry, one sec.
I've got a build compiling.

a5-29-04
00:05:06.917 --> 00:05:08.667
MAS: It's two in the morning, Gerg.

a5-29-05.1
00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:11.958
GERG: Best time there is.
Nobody else is pushing anything.

a5-29-05.2
00:05:12.042 --> 00:05:15.708
Anyway, that's not why I called.
You've got the staff letter open?

a5-29-05.3
00:05:15.792 --> 00:05:17.125
Scroll down.

a5-29-06.1
00:05:17.875 --> 00:05:20.792
They're telling the board they're
“…unable to work for or with people

a5-29-06.2
00:05:20.875 --> 00:05:25.042
that lack competence, judgement and
care for our mission and employees.”

a5-29-07
00:05:25.125 --> 00:05:28.208
And they'll quit, “…unless all
current board members resign…”

a5-29-08
00:05:28.292 --> 00:05:29.917
MAS: And go to Macrosoft.

a5-29-09
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.292
GERG: Yep. Macrosoft's promised them
“…positions for all NopeAI employees…”

a5-29-10
00:05:34.375 --> 00:05:36.042
MAS: That's a lot of desks.

a5-29-11
00:05:36.125 --> 00:05:37.713
GERG: Scroll to the bottom.

a5-29-12
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:39.875
Alyi signed it.

a5-29-13
00:05:40.292 --> 00:05:41.667
MAS: Alyi voted.

a5-29-14
00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.000
GERG: He did both.

sfx-14
00:05:43.083 --> 00:05:44.625
[slot whirs]

a5-29-15
00:05:44.667 --> 00:05:48.431
That'll be the share sale.
Everybody's been waiting on that one.

sfx-15
00:05:48.515 --> 00:05:49.708
[stamp thuds]

a5-29-16
00:05:49.792 --> 00:05:51.333
MAS: What are you building?

a5-29-17
00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.083
GERG: The company. Again. Just in case.

a5-29-18
00:05:55.333 --> 00:05:57.667
So. Do I tell everyone to pack?

a5-29-19
00:05:58.125 --> 00:06:00.167
MAS: Ask me when it compiles.

sfx-16
00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.625
[a key turns in a lock]

a5-29-20
00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:06.792
TASYA: Don't get up, Mas.
I won't keep you. Everyone is welcome.

a5-29-21
00:06:07.042 --> 00:06:08.208
MAS: Everyone.

a5-29-22
00:06:08.292 --> 00:06:12.167
TASYA: Yes. You first.
And there's a desk for every one of them.

a5-29-23
00:06:12.750 --> 00:06:14.292
MAS: Leave it open.

sfx-17
00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:21.000
[swing band music]

a5-29-24
00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.132
NELEH: Has anyone read the char—

sfx-18
00:06:29.208 --> 00:06:31.500
[music stops]

a5-30-01
00:06:38.875 --> 00:06:40.667
You sent three.

a5-30-02
00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:42.583
One for each day.

a5-30-03
00:06:42.875 --> 00:06:45.167
It has been four days.

a5-30-04
00:06:45.250 --> 00:06:47.208
I'm not counting today.

a5-30-05
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.208
MAS: What happens to you
if NopeAI disappears?

a5-30-06.1
00:06:54.333 --> 00:06:55.875
TASYA: Oh, we'd be fine.

a5-30-06.2
00:06:55.958 --> 00:06:58.958
…we have all the IP rights
and all the capability…

a5-30-06.3
00:06:59.042 --> 00:07:02.292
We are below them,
above them, around them.

a5-30-07
00:07:03.708 --> 00:07:05.473
TASYA (from the floor): Hello.

sfx-19
00:07:05.556 --> 00:07:07.375
[fire crackles]

sfx-20
00:07:07.417 --> 00:07:10.500
[door bangs open]

a5-30-08
00:07:10.625 --> 00:07:12.750
Which room is on fire?

a5-30-09
00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:14.958
…Ah.

a5-30-10.1
00:07:15.833 --> 00:07:19.333
Before this goes out, I'm reading
it once, so nobody's surprised.

a5-30-10.2
00:07:19.417 --> 00:07:22.875
We have reached an agreement in principle
for Mas Manalt to return to NopeAI

a5-30-10.3
00:07:22.958 --> 00:07:27.917
as CEO with a new initial board of Terb
(Chair), the Other Yrral, and Mada.

a5-30-11
00:07:28.292 --> 00:07:29.708
You're staying?

a5-30-12
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:33.250
He stays.
You and Gerg don't sit on the board.

a5-30-13
00:07:33.333 --> 00:07:34.542
We'll stand.

a5-30-14
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:37.292
And there'll be an independent review.

a5-30-15
00:07:37.375 --> 00:07:38.625
Of what?

sfx-21
00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:39.625
[music stops]

a5-30-16
00:07:39.708 --> 00:07:41.125
MADA: Good question.

a5-30-17
00:07:41.542 --> 00:07:43.000
MAS: Good question.

a5-30-18
00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:56.500
TTEMME: Chat, we're so back.

sfx-22
00:07:56.583 --> 00:07:59.833
[glass shatters; neon buzzes on]

sfx-23
00:08:02.875 --> 00:08:04.500
[error tone]

a5-30-19
00:08:05.958 --> 00:08:07.208
MAS: Okay.

sfx-24
00:08:07.792 --> 00:08:11.208
[low hum]

a5-31-01
00:08:11.375 --> 00:08:12.417
Is it ready?

a5-31-02
00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.000
It's a preview.

a5-31-03
00:08:14.083 --> 00:08:16.025
You said that about the last one.

a5-31-04.1
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.125
MAS: I love and respect Alyi,

a5-31-04.2
00:08:24.208 --> 00:08:28.833
I think he's a guiding light of the
field and a gem of a human being.

a5-31-04.3
00:08:28.917 --> 00:08:31.875
I harbor zero ill will towards him.

